## `copilot-instructions.md` — project-wide context

Loaded automatically into **every** Copilot chat for this workspace. It tells the
assistant about:

- Project name, tech stack, and directory layout
- Coding conventions specific to `{{ project_name }}`
- How commands/modules are structured
{% if db_driver != "none" %}- Database layer (`{{ db_driver }}`{% if db_abstraction != "none" %} + {{ db_abstraction }}{% endif %})
{% endif %}{% if cli_support != "none" %}- CLI framework (`{{ cli_support }}`) and command registration
{% endif %}
**You should keep this file up to date** as the project evolves — add new modules,
change patterns, or update tech choices here so Copilot always has accurate context.

---

## `instructions/` — per-filetype rules

Instruction files use an `applyTo` frontmatter pattern so VS Code automatically
activates them for matching file types:

| File | Applies to | Content |
|---|---|---|
| `python.instructions.md` | `**/*.py` | Python coding style, imports, type hints |
{% if testing_frameworks %}| `test.instructions.md` | `tests/**/*.py` | Test patterns, mock usage, fixtures |
{% endif %}{% if db_driver not in ("none", "nosql") or docker == "docker" %}| `bash.instructions.md` | `**/*.sh` | Shell script style, error handling |
{% endif %}{% if db_driver not in ("none", "nosql") %}| `sql.instructions.md` | `**/*.sql` | SQL style, migration conventions |
{% endif %}{% if docker == "docker" %}| `docker.instructions.md` | `**/Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose*.yml` | Docker best practices |
{% endif %}
These are loaded automatically in VS Code when you open a file that matches the
`applyTo` pattern — no manual action needed.

