## `prompts/` — reusable prompt templates

### `new-feature.prompt.md` — scaffold a new feature

Runs in `ask` mode (interactive, asks clarifying questions before writing code).

**To use:** Open it with `@workspace /prompts/new-feature.prompt.md` or click
the prompt file in VS Code and run it from the editor toolbar.

You will be prompted for a feature name. The prompt then guides Copilot to:
- Create implementation files under `src/{{ pkg_name }}/`
{% if cli_support != "none" %}- Register a CLI command (if the feature exposes one)
{% endif %}{% if db_driver not in ("none", "nosql") %}- Create migration files (if a DB table is needed)
{% endif %}{% if testing_frameworks %}- Add tests
{% endif %}{% if env_parsing != "none" %}- Add env vars to `.env.example`
{% endif %}
### `plan-feature.prompt.md` — plan before building

Runs in `feature-planner` agent mode — research only, no file edits.

Use this when you want a detailed plan to review *before* Copilot touches any code.
Enter the feature name when prompted and the planner will return a full checklist.

