## `hooks/hooks.json` — Copilot lifecycle hooks

Automatically loaded by VS Code when you open this workspace. Active hooks:

| Event | Action |
|---|---|
| `PostToolUse` (file edit) | Syntax-check edited `.py` files with `py_compile`; alert if broken |
{% if db_driver not in ("none", "nosql") %}| `PreToolUse` (shell command) | Block destructive SQL (`DROP TABLE`, `TRUNCATE`, etc.) without confirmation |
{% endif %}
These run silently in the background — you'll only see a notification if a check fails.
{% if git %}
### `hooks/pre-commit` — git hook

Installed at `.github/hooks/pre-commit` (not `.git/hooks/`). To activate it:

```bash
cp .github/hooks/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit
chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-commit
```

Once active it will **block commits** that contain Python syntax errors.
{% endif %}

